# Coming-Off PCT Sequence

> [!abstract] Owns the coming-off decision tree.
> Product owners include [[HCG renjian (10×2000IU) — Overseas GMP]], [[HCG livzon (10×4000IU) — Overseas GMP]], [[Clomiphene Clomiplin (50mg×50tab) — kohohpharma]], [[Clomiphene Clomid PharmaQo (50mg×50tab) — anabolicpharmacist]], [[Tamoxifen (20mg×30tab) — kohohpharma]], and [[Tamoxifen PharmaQo (25mg×50tab) — anabolicpharmacist]].

> [!danger] Boundary
> PCT is medical endocrine recovery. This protocol is a sequence/checklist layer, not an unsupervised dosing protocol. Ester clearance, labs, symptoms, fertility goals, and clinician review decide timing.

## What This Protocol Owns

- Whether the user is actually coming off or simply changing cycle/cruise design.
- Timing logic between suppressive compounds clearing, gonadotropin decisions, and SERM decisions.
- Recovery monitoring and failure-to-recover triggers.
- Stock math for HCG, clomiphene, tamoxifen, and support layer.

## Owned Products

- Gonadotropin lane: [[HCG renjian (10×2000IU) — Overseas GMP]], [[HCG livzon (10×4000IU) — Overseas GMP]]
- SERM lane: [[Clomiphene Clomiplin (50mg×50tab) — kohohpharma]], [[Clomiphene Clomid PharmaQo (50mg×50tab) — anabolicpharmacist]], [[Tamoxifen (20mg×30tab) — kohohpharma]], [[Tamoxifen PharmaQo (25mg×50tab) — anabolicpharmacist]]
- Support layer: [[PCT Support Layer Protocol]]

## Entry Criteria

All should be true:

- A real "coming off" decision has been made and the next suppressive block is not already scheduled.
- The last suppressive compound, ester, oral, peptide, and ancillary context is written.
- Baseline labs are available or scheduled.
- Fertility goal is clarified: general recovery versus active conception attempt.
- Sleep, nutrition, training deload, and stress controls are ready through [[PCT Support Layer Protocol]].

## Sequence Logic

1. **Confirm the off-ramp.** If the plan is cruise/change compounds, this is not PCT.
2. **Clear suppressive background.** PCT timing depends on the pharmacology of what was used. Starting recovery drugs while suppressive levels remain high can make labs harder to interpret.
3. **Gonadotropin question.** If HCG is used, it is a testicular stimulation phase that must not blur into the SERM interpretation window.
4. **SERM question.** Clomiphene/tamoxifen belong only when the goal is pituitary/HPTA stimulation and safety gates are satisfied.
5. **Verify recovery.** Symptoms are not enough. Labs and sustained function matter.

## Monitoring

- Labs: total testosterone, free testosterone, LH, FSH, estradiol, prolactin if indicated, CBC/CMP/lipids as context.
- Symptoms: libido, erectile function, mood, sleep, energy, testicular size/ache, nipple symptoms, acne, vision changes, clot symptoms.
- Training: strength retention, fatigue, injury risk, deload compliance.
- Support: protein, calories, micronutrients, sleep, and stress via [[PCT Support Layer Protocol]].

## Red Flags

Stop and seek review for visual disturbances on clomiphene, chest pain, calf swelling/pain, shortness of breath, severe mood disturbance, suicidal ideation, severe gynecomastia symptoms, jaundice, severe abdominal pain, or allergic/injection-site reaction.

## Exit Criteria

Exit when:

- Labs show acceptable recovery for the user's goal and symptoms are stable.
- A clinician changes the strategy because recovery is not occurring.
- Fertility becomes the primary goal and the plan moves to [[Fertility Push Protocol]].
- Side effects make the current sequence unacceptable.

## Stock Math

- **HCG:** total IU demand by calendar only after clinician-reviewed plan exists.
- **Clomiphene/tamoxifen:** tablet demand by active days and tablet strength; do not mix 20mg/25mg/50mg products without converting.
- **Support layer:** project D3, zinc, boron, magnesium, glycine, methyl B complex, food, and sleep supports for the entire recovery window.
- **Labs:** lab cadence is part of PCT cost planning.

